  "question": {
    "text": "Two aeroplanes I and II bomb a target in succession. The probabilities of I and II scoring a hit correctly are $0.3$ and $0.2$, respectively. The second plane will bomb only if the first misses the target. The probability that the target is hit by the second plane is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "o20N7",
      "text": "\n$0.06$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LQm8Y",
      "text": "\n$0.14$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NCABt",
      "text": "\n$0.2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7ALsF",
      "text": "\nNone of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The desired probability\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =0.7 \\times 0.2+(0.7)(0.8)(0.7)(0.2)+(0.7)(0.8)(0.7)(0.8)(0.7)(0.2)+\\ldots . \\\\\n& =0.14\\left[1+(0.56)+(0.56)^2+\\ldots\\right] \\\\\n& =0.14\\left[\\frac{1}{1-0.56}\\right]=\\frac{0.14}{0.44}=\\frac{7}{22}.\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
